---
// A title page.
//
// The old opening was a landing page: name at 4.6rem beside an autoplaying film
// that ran off the right edge, with a soft green glow behind both. Two subjects
// competing in the first viewport, and the glow was the single clearest tell
// that this was a page about AI rather than a page by an engineer.
//
// A monograph opens on one thing, set in ink, with air around it. The name is
// the subject and nothing else is on the sheet. The film has gone to the hunr
// page, where it is evidence for something instead of decoration for everything.
//
// This is the only place on the site where type is allowed to be loud, because a
// name is the one thing on a personal site that does not need qualifying.
---
<section class="masthead chamber">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="stamp">
      <span>AI systems engineer</span>
      <span>Bengaluru · UTC+5:30</span>
    </p>

    <div class="title rv">
      <h1 class="d d-1">Amartya&nbsp;Gaur</h1>
      <p class="sub">I build the layer AI agents run on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="say rv">
      <p>Five years of that was inside Newfold Digital&rsquo;s AI Center of Excellence: a{' '}
        <a href="/work/agent-orchestration/">sticky orchestrator</a> carrying about a thousand support
        conversations an hour, and <a href="/work/eval-gate/">739 regression cases</a> wired into the deploy
        pipeline so a prompt edit can fail a build. Since August 2026 it has been{' '}
        <a href="https://hunr.ai" rel="noopener">hunr.ai</a>, which I write on my own.</p>

      <p class="quiet">I also spent about 230,000 model calls trying to disprove my own routing design.
        Seven of ten pre-registered experiments{' '}
        <a href="/work/routing-benchmark/">came back negative</a>.
        That half is in this index too, because it is the more useful half.</p>

      <p class="links">
        <a href="#index">The index</a>
        <a href="/ask">Ask this site</a>
        <a href="mailto:amartya@hunr.ai">amartya@hunr.ai</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/amartya-dev" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/amartya-gaur" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- The band closes on a graduated scale rather than a rule, because the six
       years underneath the index are the first measurement in the document. -->
  <div class="scale wrap" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="tickrule"></div>
    <p class="years mono"><span>2020</span><span>2021</span><span>2022</span><span>2023</span
      ><span>2024</span><span>2025</span><span>2026</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .masthead { padding-top: clamp(104px, 12vw, 150px); }

  /* A colophon line above a hairline: what this document is, and where it was
     set. Printed matter identifies itself before it starts talking. */
  .stamp {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-dark);
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: .11em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--bone-3);
  }

  .title { margin-top: clamp(48px, 8vw, 104px); }
  h1 { color: var(--bone); }

  /* The subtitle of a title page, in italic serif. It is the claim; everything
     under it is the evidence for the claim. */
  .sub {
    margin-top: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 30px);
    font-family: var(--display); font-optical-sizing: auto;
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 380;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.9vw, 2.35rem); line-height: 1.24; letter-spacing: -.014em;
    color: var(--bone-2); max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .say {
    margin-top: clamp(46px, 6vw, 76px);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .say p { color: var(--bone-2); line-height: 1.7; }
  .say p + p { margin-top: 1.1em; }
  .quiet { color: var(--bone-dim) !important; }
  .say a { color: var(--bone); }
  .quiet a { color: var(--bone-2); }

  .links {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 28px;
    margin-top: clamp(36px, 4.4vw, 56px) !important;
    padding-top: var(--s-3); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-dark);
    font-size: var(--t-small) !important;
  }
  .links a { color: var(--bone-2) !important; }
  .links a:hover { color: var(--fail-lit) !important; }

  .scale { padding-top: clamp(52px, 7vw, 92px); padding-bottom: 30px; }
  /* The rule runs past the last label, because 2026 is not the end of the scale. */
  .scale .tickrule { width: auto; margin-right: calc(50% - 50vw); }
  .years {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--bone-3); font-size: var(--t-micro); letter-spacing: .04em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .sub { max-width: none; }
    .years span:nth-child(even) { visibility: hidden; }
  }
</style>
